7592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding Lowest Common Multiples Using Prime Factorization" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083445 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "38aff8ec-fcf4-52b8-8557-cb2bcff71738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1045 "The Triangle Inequality" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083455 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "44d765ee-f9a3-51fd-a9fb-673e5f0fd77d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083783 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186081629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083783 #edb/ref 1069 "q-53065" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083783 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083783 #edb/ref 1071 "Captain Sparrow's ship is $150\\,\\text{km}$ away from a lighthouse, while Captain Jones' ship is at a distance of $450\\,\\text{km}$ from the same lighthouse. Assuming that the three locations form a triangle, what is the range of all possible values for the distance between the two ships?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083783 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6eff57b7-61f0-5d4f-bfb7-25538940239e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083783 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we let: \n\n- $S$ be the position of Captain Sparrow's ship\n\n- $J$ be the position of Captain Jones' ship\n\n- $L$ be the position of the lighthouse\n\nLet's draw $△SJL.$\n\n![](images/da/daa3d50135304457e258e3f702a115162a085a4c3940070b4ac3cef77d5ae748.png)\n\nWe know that\n\n$$\nSL=150\\,\\text{km},\\,JL=450\\,\\text{km}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the triangle inequality theorem,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}JL-SL & <JS<JL+SL \\\\ 450-150 & <JS<450+150 \\\\ 300 & <JS<600.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance from Captain Sparrow's to Captain Jones' ship must be *between $300\\,\\text{km}$ and $600\\,\\text{km}$*." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084021 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084021 #edb/ref 1061 143346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084021 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22b878ba-aa9a-5218-889c-006c8dcacca7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084021 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084022 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084022 #edb/ref 1061 143347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084022 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5234accd-01b6-501e-866d-11b931397534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084022 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084023 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084023 #edb/ref 1061 143351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084023 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "adba60f0-2f20-5985-8599-c86e9